# Insurance Claims Intelligence Platform

## Scope
- Phase 1 frontend only — no RAG, AI agents, MCP, or backend yet
- Work incrementally, one task at a time
- Do not build the entire application in one response

## Stack
- React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- React Router, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Zod, Lucide React
- No proprietary AI-platform dependencies

## Architecture
- Separate pages, components, layouts, services, types, hooks, utils, mock data
- Business logic in services/hooks/utils — not in UI components
- Mock data in `src/mock/` — never inline in pages
- Services in `src/services/` — stub now, FastAPI later

## Types & Constants
- Use shared types from `src/types/`
- Claim statuses via `ClaimStatus` union in `src/constants/claims.ts`
- User roles: customer, agent, admin

## UI
- Enterprise insurance dashboard aesthetic
- Desktop-first, responsive, accessible forms
- Reuse layout components from `src/components/layout/`

## Commits
- Conventional commits: feat:, fix:, refactor:, docs:, test:, chore:
- Do not commit unless explicitly asked
